# Round XXV Track D §D-3: do-EXPRESSION variant of the compound-tail
# borrow-bind. `auto r = do:` newline `&a` — D10(a) `E_LocalBorrowBind`
# fires at the outer decl (authoritative). ⚠ The multi-line `do:` form is
# mandatory — the inline `do: &a` shorthand is a parse error and would
# "pass" for the wrong reason. Pre-fix the safety-pass mirror-walker also
# emitted `E_AmpInOperandPosition` on the tail `&a`; post-fix the flag
# gates the mirror-walker emit, so the fixture asserts single-diagnostic
# (E_LocalBorrowBind present, E_AmpInOperandPosition ABSENT).

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    auto r = do:
        &a
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
